ENGLISH 85

&
\newpage
\begin{verbatim}
%
% RULE RSRelMarking
< m1: CLAUSE{CLAUSErec1}
            [ mu1, 
              I1:rel1/T1, 
              mu2
            ] 
>

< m : CLAUSE{CLAUSErec1}
            [ mu1, 
              I2:rel1/T2, 
              mu2 
            ] 
>

   MATCHCONDITIONS
      <
       I1: T1.CAT IN [NPVAR, PREPPVAR, ADVPVAR] 
                     WITH T1.REC.index = indexpar
       I2: T2.CAT IN [NPVAR, PREPPVAR, ADVPVAR] 
                     WITH T2.REC.mood IN [relativexpmood, topicmood]
      >

   PARAMETERS
      <
       indexpar   : indextype
       xpmoodpar  : xpmoodtype
      >

<
   SUBRULE (* 1. NPVAR *)
      < T1:NPVAR{NPVARrec1} >
      < T2:NPVAR{NPVARrec2} >

      COMP
         <
          C1: [NPVARrec1.NPhead] * [itNP] = [] AND
              NPVARrec1.mood = nowh AND
              xpmoodpar IN [relativexpmood, topicmood] 
            C11: ((rel1 = subjrel) -> (xpmoodpar <> topicmood))
            A11: NPVARrec2 := NPVARrec1;
                 NPVARrec2.mood := xpmoodpar
            C12: rel1 = subjrel AND
                 xpmoodpar = topicmood
            A12: NPVARrec2 := NPVARrec1
                 (* mood remains nowh *)
          A1: @
         >

      DECOMP
         <
          C1: [NPVARrec1.NPhead] * [itNP] = [] AND
              ((rel1 = subjrel) -> (NPVARrec2.mood <> topicmood))
            C11: NPVARrec2.mood = relativexpmood
            A11: @
            C12: NPVARrec2.mood = topicmood
            A12: WBONUS -10;
                 @
          A1: indexpar  := NPVARrec2.index; 
              xpmoodpar := NPVARrec2.mood;
              NPVARrec1 := NPVARrec2;
              NPVARrec1.mood := nowh;
         >

   SUBRULE (* 2. PREPPVAR *)
      < T1: PREPPVAR{PREPPVARrec1} >
      < T2: PREPPVAR{PREPPVARrec2} >

      COMP
         <
          C1: rel1 <> leftdislocrel
            C11: PREPPVARrec1.mood = relativexpmood AND
                 xpmoodpar = relativexpmood
            A11: @
            C12: PREPPVARrec1.mood = nowh AND
                 xpmoodpar = relativexpmood
            A12: @
            C13: PREPPVARrec1.mood = nowh AND
                 xpmoodpar = topicmood
            A13: @
          A1: PREPPVARrec2 := PREPPVARrec1;
              PREPPVARrec2.mood := xpmoodpar
          C2: rel1 = leftdislocrel
          A2: PREPPVARrec2 := PREPPVARrec1
         >

      DECOMP
         <
          C1: true
            C11: PREPPVARrec2.mood = relativexpmood
            A11: PREPPVARrec1 := PREPPVARrec2;
            C12: PREPPVARrec2.mood = relativexpmood
            A12: PREPPVARrec1 := PREPPVARrec2;
                 PREPPVARrec1.mood := nowh;
            C13: PREPPVARrec2.mood = topicmood
            A13: WBONUS -1;
                 PREPPVARrec1 := PREPPVARrec2;
                 PREPPVARrec1.mood := nowh;
          A1: indexpar  := PREPPVARrec2.index; 
              xpmoodpar := PREPPVARrec2.mood;
         >

   SUBRULE (* 3. ADVPVAR *)
      < T1: ADVPVAR{ADVPVARrec1} >
      < T2: ADVPVAR{ADVPVARrec2} >

      COMP
         <
          C1: ADVPVARrec1.mood = nowh AND
              xpmoodpar IN [relativexpmood, topicmood] AND
              rel1 <> leftdislocrel
          A1: ADVPVARrec2 := ADVPVARrec1;
              ADVPVARrec2.mood := xpmoodpar;
          C2: ADVPVARrec1.mood = nowh AND
              xpmoodpar IN [relativexpmood, topicmood] AND
              rel1 = leftdislocrel
          A2: ADVPVARrec2 := ADVPVARrec1
         >

      DECOMP
         <
          C1: true
            C11: ADVPVARrec2.mood = relativexpmood
            A11: @
            C12: ADVPVARrec2.mood = topicmood
            A12: WBONUS -1;
                 @
          A1: indexpar  := ADVPVARrec2.index; 
              xpmoodpar := ADVPVARrec2.mood;
              ADVPVARrec1 := ADVPVARrec2;
              ADVPVARrec1.mood := nowh;
         >
>
&

\end{verbatim}
\newpage
\begin{description}
\item[* name:] RSRelMarking
\item[* relevant examples:] \mbox{}\\
NPVAR: (The man) x1=who came in from the cold\\
PREPPVAR: (the river) he swims x1=in which; note that there are two subrules 
for relatives: in case there is a CNVAR in the PREPP (restrictive relative), 
the mood already has been set to relative; in case there is an NPVAR (non-
restrictive, or relative of NP that has no CN-level), the mood is still nowh. 
In analysis, this causes two paths to 
originate from here; this can be remedied by using the special `dakje'-
construction, allowing one to look `into the variable'. However, this has not 
been implemented yet, since the wrong path will run dry anyway.\\
ADVPVAR: x1=homewards she ran\\
Perhaps also relatives: ??(the place) he swims x1=where?? (this will perhaps 
be analysed as 
`the place at which'; there may be a translation problem if the Dutch has an 
adverb as antecedent and not the 
NP `the place': {\em daar waar er problemen rijzen,...\/} $\rightarrow$ {\em 
where(ever) problems arise,...\/}); however, the relative subrule has been 
formulated anyway, since it will do no harm. 
\item[* language:] (Dutch, English, Spanish) English
\item[* kind of rule:] (M-rule, S-rule, Transferrule) M-rule
\item[* subgrammar:] CLAUSEtoSENTENCE
\item[* class:] (name of rule, transformation or filter class) RC\_RelMarking
\item[* date of creation:] 3-OCT-1988
\item[* author:] margreet sanders
\item[* copied from:] Dutch Rrelmarking1
\item[* modification:]\mbox{}
\begin{enumerate}
\item date: 25/09/89\ \ \ \ \ author: Margreet Sanders\\
Added subrules for PREPP/ADVPVAR, and added conditions on topicmood
\item date: 05/10/89\ \ \ \ \ author: Margreet Sanders\\
Added CA-pair for `topicalised subject NPs' in generation of subrule 1; default 
rule, to let structures in which the subject is supposed to topicalise because 
it was not a subject in the source language (e.g.\ for ergatives like `please') 
pass this rule class, though no relmarking is done.
\item date: 11/10/89\ \ \ \ \ author: Margreet Sanders\\
Added CA-pairs in generation of subrules 2-3 for leftdislocrel constituents 
(sentadvs), because they should not get any relmarking (they need not shift).
\item date: ../../..\ \ \ \ \ author:
\end{enumerate}
\item[* task:] to give the variable that will be spelled out as a relative or 
that will be topicalised the 
appropriate mood (if still necessary: PPs have already received relativemood 
when there is a CNVAR under it). The actual shifting will be done in 
TC\_WhShift.
\item[\ \ strategy:] (also: deviations from accepted proposals) note that 
the topicmood for NPs is given very low bonus, to make sure that all other 
translations are given first. The other subrules for topic mood simply receive 
a lower bonus of -1, because topicalisation in itself is a less likely process
\item[\ \ rejected alternatives:]
\item[\ \ clarification of variables:]
\item[\ \ clarification of the splitting up into subrules:]
\item[\ \ clarification of the collapsing of rules:] (e.g. clarification of parameters)
